<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Projects hold todos. Todos can depend on other todos, and a todo you are
    waiting on is one you cannot tick off yet — Telos knows that and says so.
    You run it yourself: one container plus Postgres, with the app and the API
    on the same origin. AI is off unless you turn it on.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Dependencies</h3>
        <p>A blocked todo sits in its own section with its blockers named and its checkbox disabled, and cycles are rejected when you try to create them.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>A board, or a list</h3>
        <p>The same todos as columns you name yourself, one of which means done: drag a card there and it is ticked off.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Labels</h3>
        <p>One colour, one name, attachable to projects and todos alike.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Save the <code>docker-compose.yml</code> from the
      <a href="{{ site.repo }}#quickstart" rel="noopener">README's Quickstart</a>
      in an empty directory, then generate the two secrets it needs and bring it up:
    </p>
    <pre class="code"><code>printf 'AUTH_SECRET=%s\nPOSTGRES_PASSWORD=%s\n' \
  "$(openssl rand -hex 32)" "$(openssl rand -hex 24)" &gt; .env

docker compose up -d</code></pre>
    <p>
      Telos is then on <code>http://localhost:3001</code>. Migrations run at
      boot. The magic link to sign in goes to the log:
      <code>docker compose logs -f telos</code>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
    Full documentation lives in the project README:
    <a href="{{ site.repo }}#readme" rel="noopener">{{ site.repo }}</a>
    {% if site.docker %}<br />The image is
    <a href="{{ site.docker }}" rel="noopener">vantreeseba/telos on Docker Hub</a>.{% endif %}
  </p>
</section>
